{
  "id": "COMPOUND:4343 - PROTEIN:6150",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which Cycloleucine may interact with H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3, through a series of target relationships involving sialyltransferases. Cycloleucine is shown to target CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which is a known target of multiple compounds, including (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan and 2-Methylheptyl propanoate. These compounds are also linked to the same target, implying a possible mode of action involving the sialyltransferase. Additionally, Polygonatoside A, another compound targeting the same sialyltransferase, is also linked to H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3. This suggests that the sialyltransferase may serve as a critical mediator in the interaction between Cycloleucine and the transporter, potentially through a mechanism involving the inhibition of the transporter or the modulation of sialylation processes. The evidence supports a plausible pathway where Cycloleucine may influence the activity of the transporter via its interaction with the sialyltransferase, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm this mechanism.",
